From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] dhclient-script: Darwin's ifconfig and route

Darwin's ifconfig has no -n (FreeBSD's "don't load modules"). The ARP
flush is skipped where there is no arp. Looking for the default route
before there is one, Darwin's route prints "not in table" on standard
error, which reaches netconfigd's log; it is discarded.

The name servers go to resolvconf(8) as on FreeBSD (resolvconf_enable
YES, the default): NeoDarwin's is FreeBSD's openresolv (base/resolvconf),
whose /etc/resolvconf.conf writes the merged file to /var/run/resolv.conf
(/etc/resolv.conf links to it, as on macOS) and signals mDNSResponder.
Until P4-24's IPv6 DNS work this patch wrote /var/run/resolv.conf itself.

Rebase-risk: low (three lines).
--- a/dhclient-script
+++ b/dhclient-script
@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@
 
 ARP=/usr/sbin/arp
 HOSTNAME=/bin/hostname
-IFCONFIG='/sbin/ifconfig -n'
+IFCONFIG='/sbin/ifconfig'
 
 LOCALHOST=127.0.0.1
 
@@ -47,7 +47,8 @@
 }
 
 arp_flush() {
-	arp -an -i $interface | \
+	[ -x $ARP ] || return 0
+	$ARP -an -i $interface | \
 		sed -n -e 's/^.*(\(.*\)) at .*$/arp -d \1/p' | \
 		sh >/dev/null 2>&1
 }
@@ -276,7 +277,7 @@
 # commands that are available prior to /usr being mounted.
 is_default_interface()
 {
-	routeget="`route -n get -inet default`"
+	routeget="`route -n get -inet default 2>/dev/null`"
 	oldifs="$IFS"
 	IFS="
 "
